	(footprint "LED_D3.0mm_P5.08mm_LaserPads"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "c63a5966-0a53-462a-bd88-84b8d0265d5f")
		(at 82.88 87.08 90)
		(descr "3 mm through-hole LED on a widened 5.08 mm lead pitch. Every stock LED_THT two-pad footprint is 2.54 mm pitch with 1.8 mm pads, which leaves a 0.74 mm pad-to-pad gap -- below the 0.85 mm laser rule and well below the 1.2 mm a 0.8 mm endmill needs. LED legs bend freely, so the pitch is the lever to pull rather than the pad size: 5.08 mm with 2.0 mm pads gives a 3.08 mm channel that clears either process with room to spare. Pad 1 = K (cathode, square pad, chord on the silk body marks the flat), pad 2 = A. Silk body is drawn at 1.2 mm radius rather than the true 1.5 mm so it clears both pads by 0.34 mm -- a full-size circle lands 0.04 mm off pad 2 and trips silk_over_copper. Drill 0.8 mm suits the ~0.5 mm legs and is already the commonest drill on this board.")
		(tags "LED THT 3mm 5.08mm laser mill wide clearance")
